  "id": "embodied-cognition",
  "term": "embodied cognition",
  "definition": "Embodied cognition is the view that thinking is not confined to the brain alone but is distributed across the body and the surrounding environment. On this view, tools, spaces, and other contextual features can become part of the cognitive system, shaping understanding and reorganizing mental activity during perception and action.",
